{"availability":"available","full":"mercurjs/mercur","name":"mercur","description":"The complete open source platform to run your entire marketplace. Storefront, vendor panel, admin console, and integrations in one enterprise-grade platform you own.","category":"Business","language":"TypeScript","stars":1830,"forks":463,"created":"2024-04-23T15:36:13Z","updated":"2026-10-05T16:15:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.mercurjs.com","topics":["b2b-marketplace","composable-commerce","ecommerce","enterprise","headless-commerce","marketplace","medusa","medusajs","multi-vendor","typescript"],"demo":"https://www.mercurjs.com/enterprise","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.291Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.291Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.291Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.291Z","stars":1830,"forks":463}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The open-source marketplace platform. A Mirakl alternative.","Mercur is an open-source, headless platform for building multi-vendor marketplaces. Add vendor onboarding, multi-vendor catalogs, offers, commissions, and automated payouts on top of a commerce core you can change at its foundation. Run B2C, B2B, and hybrid marketplaces without choosing between a profit-draining SaaS platform and a build from scratch."],"features":["Own your marketplace, no fees: Self-host on your own infrastructure with full source access. No percentage of GMV, no per-transaction cut, no vendor lock-in — your data, your customers, and your roadmap stay yours.","Built for the marketplace model: Vendor onboarding, multi-vendor catalogs, offers, commissions, and automated payouts are built in — multiple sellers can list offers against the same product, so you're not rebuilding…","Headless and customizable, no forks: TypeScript, event-driven, and API-first — serve any storefront or frontend. Extend or override workflows, products, and vendor rules through a composable architecture built for the…","Standing on Medusa: Inherit a mature, battle-tested commerce core — catalog, orders, payments, shipping, tax, and stock — instead of reinventing it. Mercur adds the marketplace layer on top of Medusa.","Production-ready and AI-native: Run real marketplaces in production today, on an architecture designed for AI-assisted development — an introspectable, API-first stack that works hand in hand with your AI coding tools."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mercurjs/mercur/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5505aa9758f421f75e603fd7768dab2ac90d5ac3b0f3da32eb104038b20d7150","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.416Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.416Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The open-source marketplace platform. A Mirakl alternative.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mercurjs/mercur/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Built for the marketplace model: Vendor onboarding, multi-vendor catalogs, offers, commissions, and automated payouts are built in — multiple sellers can list offers against the same product, so you're not rebuilding…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mercurjs/mercur/blob/main/README.md"},{"text":"Headless and customizable, no forks: TypeScript, event-driven, and API-first — serve any storefront or frontend. Extend or override workflows, products, and vendor rules through a composable architecture built for the…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mercurjs/mercur/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Own your marketplace, no fees: Self-host on your own infrastructure with full source access.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mercurjs/mercur/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign in to the Vendor Panel with those credentials, or manage everything from the Admin Panel.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mercurjs/mercur/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"5505aa9758f421f75e603fd7768d